=== zone gz10g
Foothills
The foothills are the border between settled human territory and wild lands. The Free Hunters' camp is located here, but far more often than humans, goblins and orcs can be found here.

=== zone gz11d1
The Lizardmen's Tomb
In this neglected underground palace of a former civilization, the lizardfolk have arranged a tomb for their chiefs. Not a single human has managed to get here for many years.

=== zone gz11d2
Babur's Mine
An old mine where the craftsman Babur used to get material to make weapons. Then, when everything valuable was carried away, the mine ceased to function, and underground monsters settled there.
=== zone gz11g
Distant peaks
The farthest territory from the Village. People rarely visit and even more rarely return. But there is a rumor in the Village that an artisan has somehow learned how to get as far as the folds of stone that are found there.
=== zone gz12g
Cave
An underworld of greater size, having several exits to the surface. Even crude orcs have only inhabited part of the cave and do not venture into the depths, where creatures not found on the surface live.

=== zone gz13g
The way to the witch
The Witch Esther had a quarrel with the whole village and moved into a cave, a little away from the people. In order not to be bothered by curious people, she has set magical traps on the way to her abode. She also uses the trolls living in the area to protect her dwelling.
=== zone gz14g
The tunnel
The tunnel bears traces of ancient times, as do the many ruintas on Gipath. It used to be the shortest and safest way through the mountains in the gorge, but a lot has changed since then.
=== zone gz15g
Village and Ruins
This place got its name from the ruins of ancient buildings, relatively safe. But having mistaken the way, a person can get into a very unpleasant situation.
=== zone gz16g
River and islands
The river, beginning in the Distant Peaks, flows into the Great Lake, forming a delta with numerous islands. Here are many settlements of goblins and orcs, their homes and altars. Free hunters sometimes hunt here too, but they try not to stay long.

=== zone gz1d1
Rat farm
In this underground, rats are bred for their tails, which can be used as food. The underground has two exits.

=== zone gz1d2
Catacombs
Neglected catacombs through which you can exit the fortress surrounding the Portal.

=== zone gz1g
Western Castle Area
To the east of here is an inaccessible castle - the refuge of the Jygran world. This is where the dungeons from which Kira managed to escape with such difficulty are located.

=== zone gz1h
Portal
The place takes its name from an old building, but in addition to this artifact there is a fortress surrounding it, much of the town of Suslanger, and several estates.

=== zone gz21k
City surroundings
There is only one city in this province of Ingos, which is the residence of the government. People who are unfriendly towards the inhabitants of Ingos City have settled around it due to the devastating taxes imposed by the governor. In addition, creatures called the Forest People live here - after their place of residence.
=== zone gz22d1
Abandoned mines
Ore was once mined here, but after the miners in the mine reached Wormtail territory, the work was abandoned. The Lords of the Underworld do not like to be disturbed.
=== zone gz22k
Abandoned mines
The name of this place reflects its recent past - there used to be extensive mines here, but after monsters started appearing in them, the entrances were closed and the area became deserted.

=== zone gz23k
Karansula property
This is the location of Karansula's workshops. His subordinates control almost the entire territory, except for the narrow valleys between the mountain branches.

=== zone gz24k
Mines
The mines used to be used for mining gold and stones - the only source of income for the province. That's why this part of the mine is well protected, and it's better not to drop in on the guards. The other half was closed when miners violated the dwellings of underground creatures.

=== zone gz25k
Snowy wilderness
Although this place is almost uninhabited due to poor conditions, there is a small lumberjack village to the west, and it is the only safe place in the area. Sometimes the aurora borealis can be seen here.

=== zone gz26k
An old portal
In this cave there is a portal that has not been used for so long that it has been forgotten.
=== zone gz2h
The town of Suslanger and its surroundings
The town, which gave its name to all the land around it, is situated on the shore of a lake from which irrigation canals extend. The people working in the fields are unarmed, but ready to raise the alarm at the sight of strangers, or else they themselves will be threatened with punishment.

=== zone gz31j
The city of Dar-Leanos and its surroundings
This is all that remains of Cania, and even the fate of these lands is in question. The city is under attack from the undead, parasites have spread across the fields and highwaymen have taken over the passes. Despite the city's high and inaccessible walls, its demise is only a matter of time.


=== zone gz32j
Death Island
The island was once used by Cania as a naval hub - in the form of an old harbor and dilapidated warehouses that have survived to this day. Now a powerful necromancer has settled here, whose strength has caused half the island to die. On Dragon Mountain stands a symbol of human freedom, the statue of the heroic vampire destroyer.
=== zone gz33j
Fortress of Dar-Ugorn
This fortress used to belong to Cania, but was abandoned not long ago. The fortress of Dar-Ugorn was occupied by Khadagan warriors and the surrounding area was ruined. Only wraiths cultivate the fields, as necromancers have turned all the peasants into zombies. These monsters provide food for the garrisons.
=== zone gz34d1
Joon's Ancient Lair
The Ancient Joon Repository is the only vestige of the Joons in the land of Jygran. It was created and sealed with magic to keep the knowledge and artifacts of the ancient race from falling into the wrong hands.
=== zone gz34j
Two Rivers
This area got its name because of the two rivers flowing through it. Previously, there was a city in between the rivers, but the war turned it into ruins and the massacred inhabitants began to forage. The place between these rivers is strategic, which is why a powerful Cadagan camp is located in the ruins.

=== zone gz35j
Sadrok City and Surrounding Area
The city of Sadrok and the lands around it are the mainstay of the Kadagan Empire on Jygran. Numerous armies of the living and the dead have gathered in the city, and there is Castle of Firez, a working harbor, a military academy, a necromancer's guild, and the homes of aristocrats. High in the mountains to the south is the Joon Prison.

=== zone gz36j
Throne room
The throne room and treasury of the self-proclaimed ruler, the mad necromancer Firez. Here the fate of the world of Jygran will be decided. This is where the final battle with Firez will be fought.
=== zone gz3d1
Prison
This underground complex belongs to the necromancer's guild. The complex includes prison cells, a torture room, a court room and a death quarters.

=== zone gz3h
Necromancer's desert
The dwellings and laboratories of the necromancers are located in the desert, away from prying eyes. The guard barracks are also located there, which makes the protection of these facilities very real.

=== zone gz4h
The Cave of Worms
A deep cave containing the Temple of the Worm-heads, beings who wield great magical powers. The cleansing of the cave has been a very costly operation with heavy losses, so the Cadagan warriors limit themselves to guarding the exits.

=== zone gz5h
Canyon of death
This is where the training camp of the Cadagan army is located. Warriors eager to raise their rank conduct hunts for slaves, who are carried off from individual dungeons.

=== zone gz7d1
The old mine
Once upon a time, people who lived in a town nearby worked in this mine, but the town was abandoned and the mine was abandoned.

=== zone gz7d2
Goblin Mine
In this mine goblins get materials to make weapons.

=== zone gz7g
The dead city
Two mountain ridges protrude into the wide plain, separating a valley. In this valley lies the Dead City - once inhabited by humans, but now only their undead remains.
=== zone gz8g
Sands
To the east of the Great Lake stretches a sandy desert, which is bounded by mountains to the north. Several tribes of orcs live in this area, and this is also the main home of the lizardfolk. Orcs and lizardmen still compete with each other for access to water.
=== zone gz9d1
Goblin Mine
In this mine goblins get materials to make weapons.

=== zone gz9g
Middle Peaks
Mountains occupy the northern half of this area, and the southern half is much more level and comfortable for movement. The flat part is sparsely populated, and a careful traveler will be able to cross it without encountering a single enemy. The mountains are much more dangerous, and people try not to go there.

